WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:01.229
(audience cheering)
- Hello there.

00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:02.343
- Goodness hi!

00:00:02.343 --> 00:00:03.701
(audience cheering)

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:04.635
- [Kelly] I would wear that.

00:00:04.635 --> 00:00:05.590
- I would wear this.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.260
- I feel like I should
be on a beach somewhere.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.133
If we would like to just leave
now and go, it would feel-

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:11.980
- I would follow you to that beach.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.740
- Yeah, so have y'all met before?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.848
- No.
- No.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:15.681
- I don't know if you've ever met before.

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:16.514
- But I admire your work.

00:00:16.514 --> 00:00:17.347
- Likewise.

00:00:17.347 --> 00:00:18.240
- You devoured "White Lotus".

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.620
- Oh my goodness, thank you so much.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.453
I'm obsessed.

00:00:21.453 --> 00:00:22.445
This is wild.

00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:23.963
- It is a wild thing.

00:00:23.963 --> 00:00:26.330
Wait, I love finding out
that you are musical.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.900
So did you do musical theater growing up?

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:29.733
Did you?

00:00:29.733 --> 00:00:32.423
- I did, barely in high school.

00:00:32.423 --> 00:00:37.423
I'm what you call a karaoke person

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.187
versus someone who's just like,

00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:42.403
"Oh yeah, I sing professionally",
'cause it's terrifying.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.990
- But when you get terrified?

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.100
- I get terrified because I feel like-

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.600
- That's how I get acting.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.433
- What?

00:00:49.433 --> 00:00:50.920
- Exactly, I could sing in front

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.682
of billions of people and be like,

00:00:52.682 --> 00:00:53.530
(Kelly making trumpet sounds)

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.363
- [Natasha] Yeah.

00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:56.540
- But if I have to act,

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.540
I want to full on my pants.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.570
- Yes, yes, yes, yes, no, no, no, no, no.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:03.800
Clean up on aisle, me

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.239
- Clean up on aisle this.

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:06.072
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:07.300
- I get so nervous and
that's why I don't do it

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.770
'cause I don't enjoy it.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.600
- I just love the acting so much,

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.280
when I was in high school,

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.550
and so I wanted to be in everything.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.830
So it's just like the musical everything.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:19.740
But I auditioned for "Music
Man", when I was a junior.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:20.573
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:20.573 --> 00:01:23.200
- And my best friend at the
time was hearing impaired

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.570
and I wanted to understand
her world better.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.390
So I taught myself ASL.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.223
And so I was like-
- That's cool.

00:01:28.223 --> 00:01:30.290
- "I will sign the song that I sing

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.550
for this audition 'cause
at least it'll distract me

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.380
from the the pressure of singing."

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.760
- That's beautiful.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.150
- It was in theory.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.023
So-

00:01:38.023 --> 00:01:39.050
- Oh.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:42.610
- What happened was during
the audition I got nervous

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.690
as I predicted and forgot the sign

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:48.140
but my hands were in the air

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.033
and I committed by just
doing interpretive dance.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:53.128
(audience laughing)

00:01:53.128 --> 00:01:56.060
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.052
Yeah.

00:01:57.052 --> 00:01:57.885
- That's amazing.

00:01:57.885 --> 00:02:00.350
- So I just kind of danced
along to what I was singing.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.300
- You just moved your hands.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.810
- Yeah and what put it over of the edge

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.460
was the crying that happened.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.293
- Oh no.

00:02:06.293 --> 00:02:07.923
- As I was dancing with
my hands in the air.

00:02:07.923 --> 00:02:09.371
- 'Cause you were like,

00:02:09.371 --> 00:02:11.076
♪ I'm going down ♪

00:02:11.076 --> 00:02:14.380
- Yes, yes, it was rough stuff,

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.173
but I made the musical guys.

00:02:16.173 --> 00:02:17.883
(audience cheering)

00:02:17.883 --> 00:02:18.930
I made the musical.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:19.930
That's right, that's right.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.110
I was in the chorus.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.330
I was in the deep chorus.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.410
They don't create deep chorus nowadays,

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.320
but my teacher created one for me.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.170
- That's amazing, wait, have
you ever had that moment

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.360
on stage where you just,
it didn't go as planned?

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.193
- Constantly.

00:02:33.193 --> 00:02:34.026
- [Kelly] Yeah, okay.

00:02:34.026 --> 00:02:35.944
- I'm a 50, 50 actor at best.

00:02:35.944 --> 00:02:36.777
(all laughing)

00:02:36.777 --> 00:02:39.370
- Oh my God.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:40.820
I had a moment like that in high school.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.720
I had one in high school and it was like,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.927
everyone was so loud and everyone's like,

00:02:44.927 --> 00:02:46.260
"Oh she can hit whistle notes."

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.840
So I was like, "Put a
whistle note in the song."

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.860
I was like, "Okay, cool."

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.810
But they started yelling so loud

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.628
that I couldn't hear the song.

00:02:52.628 --> 00:02:53.461
- [Natasha] Oh no.

00:02:53.461 --> 00:02:55.440
- So I did hit a note just
in a key for another song.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.273
Like a key.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:02.209
And I fled to like the
closest closet I could find

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.900
and just was like, you
know, you're in high school.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.740
You're like, "It is over."

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:08.957
- Yeah, your life ends
when you mess up, yeah.

00:03:08.957 --> 00:03:10.840
- It was so big, now it's just funny.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.673
- Yes.

00:03:11.673 --> 00:03:12.506
Now I can laugh about it.

00:03:12.506 --> 00:03:13.740
- Now I'm just like-

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.028
- But I also learn like,
(Kelly screaming)

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:15.861
- It's like,

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:16.694
(Kelly screaming)

00:03:16.694 --> 00:03:18.240
- Yeah, you just, when you audition

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.620
for something, just be yourself.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.330
Don't try to do too much.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:22.500
I did not know that then.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.560
- That's kinda very thoughtful though

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.210
that you had a friend, that's really cool.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.260
- Yeah, Sarah Dubner she's
out there still, yeah.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.070
- Ah, still waiting for that performance.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:29.903
- I know.

00:03:29.903 --> 00:03:31.104
(all laughing)

00:03:31.104 --> 00:03:33.370
I'm still working on
it, still working on it.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.020
- We will do this for you, Sarah.

00:03:36.024 --> 00:03:39.080
So your new movie, I loved the
original "Sonic The Hedgehog"

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.940
was played so much in our
house, this one will as well.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.220
So thank you for that for a new movie.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.670
But the new movie, so what's it about?

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:50.420
- Well, we get to see
Sonic in a new world,

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.830
playing and doing the
things that we saw before

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.880
but it's bigger, badder and faster.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:55.713
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:55.713 --> 00:03:59.210
- My character is Rachel and
my sister is Maddie played

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.115
by the incredible Tika Sumpter.

00:04:01.115 --> 00:04:01.948
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:01.948 --> 00:04:04.555
- And my fiance is Shemar Moore.

00:04:04.555 --> 00:04:05.995
(audience cheering)

00:04:05.995 --> 00:04:06.997
- I know I'm interviewing him

00:04:06.997 --> 00:04:08.190
for the movie as well, yeah.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.010
- I may or may not have had a calendar

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.600
of him when I was 16, on my wall.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:13.670
- Dreams do come true.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:14.503
- They do.

00:04:14.503 --> 00:04:15.420
They really, really do.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.680
And so when the director called me

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.513
and he was just like,

00:04:18.513 --> 00:04:20.600
"We'd love to have you
back for the second movie.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.520
How do you feel about playing
opposite Shemar Moore?"

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.420
Then there was a Natasha size
hole in my wall where I ran.

00:04:27.406 --> 00:04:28.239
(all laughing)

00:04:28.239 --> 00:04:29.320
He's like, "We're not shooting just yet."

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.795
And then I ran back home and I was like,

00:04:30.795 --> 00:04:31.628
"All right cool."

00:04:31.628 --> 00:04:32.461
- I'm ready.

00:04:32.461 --> 00:04:33.490
- I'm ready, lets do it!

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.000
- You are so funny in the first one.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.170
So I just, literally,
I love when people make

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.730
like films like this that
are for kids and adults,

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.820
we all enjoy it at the same time.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:43.653
- It's for everybody.

00:04:43.653 --> 00:04:46.024
- It's really cool of y'all to do for us.

00:04:46.024 --> 00:04:48.160
'Cause some of them aren't for adults

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.390
and you're like, "Oh my gosh."

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:50.240
- [Natasha] Yeah.

